body:
Reading the deck's raw top-level `templates:` value from kalide.yaml — the value the library resolution needs before a theme registry exists, since deck.LoadConfig needs a theme registry that comes from the not-yet-resolved library — is defined once, in internal/deck: a single read over an `fs.FS` that returns the raw `templates:` string, or `""` when the file cannot be read, when its YAML cannot be decoded, and when the top-level `templates:` key is absent or is not a string. The empty value is what selects the deck-root `templates/` layer (layered-template-library). internal/deck is the lowest-level package every call site already imports and it owns kalide.yaml's `ConfigFile`, so the one read has a home all its callers share (global.constraint.shared-helpers-single-home). Every call site that reads the raw value calls this one read:

- the reload pipeline (internal/server/reload.go, server.configuredTemplates);
- the file watcher (internal/watch/watch.go, watch.configuredTemplates);
- the CLI's library resolution in each of the four commands that resolve a library before loading the deck — internal/cli/start.go, internal/cli/templates.go, internal/cli/check.go and internal/cli/render.go;
- the two CLI test helpers that load a deck a command wrote — internal/cli/upgrade_test.go's `assertUpgradeDeckLoads` and internal/cli/init_test.go's `assertInitDeckLoads` — both reading the raw value through the one read.

Two neighbouring reads keep their own definitions and are not this one. internal/scaffold/refresh.go's `scaffold.refreshDeckConfig` reads the value through a `yaml:"templates"` struct field and returns its own read and parse errors — `upgrade: read …` for an unreadable kalide.yaml and `upgrade: parse …` for a malformed one — rather than the empty value. internal/scaffold/external.go's `externalConfig` struct is the write-side read of the marshalled `title` and `templates` fields `kalide init <path>` writes, not the raw `templates:` read the library resolution uses.

AC:
- the raw `templates:` read is defined once in internal/deck and the reload pipeline, the file watcher, the CLI's four library-resolving commands and the two CLI test helpers each read the raw value through that one read;
- a config that cannot be read, cannot be decoded, or has no `templates:` key yields the empty value that selects the deck-root `templates/` layer;
- `scaffold.refreshDeckConfig` reads the value through its own struct field and returns its own read and parse errors for an unreadable or malformed kalide.yaml;
- internal/scaffold/external.go's `externalConfig` struct is the write-side read of the marshalled `title` and `templates` fields, not the raw read.
